# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out as CRLF while the
# committed blobs are LF. Prettier is configured for LF, so `pnpm format:check` then fails on
# every file for a reason that has nothing to do with the code, and passes in CI on Linux. Pinning
# the working tree to LF makes the local check agree with CI on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git should never touch.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# Generated; keep out of diffs.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
